  I logged the skipped review in the ungated ledger.

  [1mMain design choice:[0m the page is built from the kit that came with the Keel admin template, in [38;5;153mvendor/kit/[39m. It does not
  copy the hand-written markup in [38;5;153mservices.js[39m. The kit already does what the spec asks for:
  - [1mHeader:[0m [38;5;153mpageHeader[39m shows "Deploys" with the snapshot time under it.
  - [1mFilter:[0m [38;5;153mfilterBar[39m with [38;5;153mselectField[39m gives the environment dropdown, and its [38;5;153mkeep[39m option carries the sort through a
    filter change.
  - [1mTable:[0m [38;5;153mdataTable[39m handles the column sorting with the same links and ▲▼ arrows as Services, and switches to an
    empty-state message when nothing matches.
  - [1mStatus chips:[0m [38;5;153mbadge[39m has [38;5;153mok[39m/[38;5;153mbad[39m/[38;5;153mwarn[39m/[38;5;153minfo[39m colors that are exactly green/red/amber/blue in [38;5;153mkit.css[39m, so no CSS changes
    are needed.

  I read "behave as on the Services page" as being about behavior (query parameters, defaults, filter and sort keeping
  each other), not about the markup.

  [1mTasks:[0m
